Subject: [PATCH 1/2] media: ov5693: add the OVTI5693 ACPI HID

Carried verbatim from linux-surface, patches/6.19/0013-cameras.patch, which is
the only hunk that series applies to this file. Surface firmware names the front
sensor OVTI5693 rather than the INT33BE the mainline table matches, so without
this the driver never binds.

Reproduce: the running in-tree module already carries it --
  modinfo ov5693 | grep OVTI5693  ->  alias: acpi*:OVTI5693:*
Dropping it here would regress binding relative to the stock module.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
@@ -1396,6 +1396,7 @@
 
 static const struct acpi_device_id ov5693_acpi_match[] = {
 	{"INT33BE"},
+	{"OVTI5693"},
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, ov5693_acpi_match);
